[[Open This|Install Docker in Ubuntu]]

---

https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/ubuntu/

Uninstall OLD:

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo apt-get remove docker docker-engine docker.io containerd runc">>

```bash
sudo apt-get remove docker docker-engine docker.io containerd runc
```

---

Set up repo:

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo apt-get update">>
`sudo apt-get update`

<<copy-to-clipboard """
sudo apt-get install \
    ca-certificates \
    curl \
    gnupg \
    lsb-release
""">>

```bash
sudo apt-get install \
    ca-certificates \
    curl \
    gnupg \
    lsb-release
```

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings">>
`sudo mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings`

<<copy-to-clipboard """
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
""">>
```bash
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
```

<<copy-to-clipboard """
echo \
  "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu \
  $(lsb_release -cs) stable" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null
""">>
```bash
echo \
  "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu \
  $(lsb_release -cs) stable" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null
```

Install Docker Engine:

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo apt-get update">>
`sudo apt-get update`

<<copy-to-clipboard """
sudo apt-get install docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
""">>
```bash
sudo apt-get install docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
```

<<<GPG Error?
```bash
sudo chmod a+r /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
```
<<<

<<<To install a specific version of Docker Engine, list the available versions in the repo, then select and install:

<<copy-to-clipboard "apt-cache madison docker-ce">>
`apt-cache madison docker-ce`

Example: `docker-ce | 5:27.5.1-1~ubuntu.24.04~noble | https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu noble/stable amd64 Packages`

<<copy-to-clipboard """
sudo apt-get install docker-ce=<VERSION_STRING> docker-ce-cli=<VERSION_STRING> containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
""">>
```
sudo apt-get install docker-ce=<VERSION_STRING> docker-ce-cli=<VERSION_STRING> containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
```
<<<

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo service docker start">>
`sudo service docker start`

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo docker run hello-world">>
`sudo docker run hello-world`

---

Uninstall docker

<<copy-to-clipboard """
sudo apt-get purge docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
""">>

```bash
sudo apt-get purge docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
```

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo rm -rf /var/lib/docker">>
`sudo rm -rf /var/lib/docker`

<<copy-to-clipboard "sudo rm -rf /var/lib/containerd">>
`sudo rm -rf /var/lib/containerd`
